     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Even 3,000 mg/day is the highest dose seen in some references. A 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per administration. At this dose there is a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual max.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
      }
     ],
